<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{e^{s_{2}}}{\left(\frac{s}{s_{1}}\right)^{s}}\right)^{d}&lt;\frac{1}{e3d^{3}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{e^{s_{2}}}{\left(\frac{s}{s_{1}}\right)^{s}}\right)^{d}&lt;\frac{1}{e3d^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">In order to prove the last inequality above, it is enough to set <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{3}=e^{s_{2}}/(\frac{s}{s_{1}})^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{3}=e^{s_{2}}/(\frac{s}{s_{1}})^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{s}(d)=d^{3}(s_{3})^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{s}(d)=d^{3}(s_{3})^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and note that <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{s}(54000)&lt;0.1&lt;1/(3e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>54000</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{s}(54000)&lt;0.1&lt;1/(3e)</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing for <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> at least <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/\ln(s_{3}^{-1})&lt;4613" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4613</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/\ln(s_{3}^{-1})&lt;4613</annotation></semantics></math>, which follows by a standard analysis of the first derivative of <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(S_{v}~|~\bigcap_{B\in\mathcal{B}}\overline{B}\right)\leq\mathbb{P}\left(d_{S^{*}}(v)\geq sd~|~\bigcap_{B\in\mathcal{B}}\overline{B}\right)=\mathbb{P}\left(d_{S^{*}}(v)\geq sd\right)&lt;\frac{1}{e3d^{3}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(S_{v}~|~\bigcap_{B\in\mathcal{B}}\overline{B}\right)\leq\mathbb{P}\left(d_{S^{*}}(v)\geq sd~|~\bigcap_{B\in\mathcal{B}}\overline{B}\right)=\mathbb{P}\left(d_{S^{*}}(v)\geq sd\right)&lt;\frac{1}{e3d^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The analysis concerning <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is analogous. Set</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{*}=\left\{vw\in E:1\leq|O_{v}-O_{w}|_{K}\leq\frac{sd+7}{2}\vee 1\leq|I_{v}-I_{w}|_{K}\leq\frac{sd+7}{2}\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>∨</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{*}=\left\{vw\in E:1\leq|O_{v}-O_{w}|_{K}\leq\frac{sd+7}{2}\vee 1\leq|I_{v}-I_{w}|_{K}\leq\frac{sd+7}{2}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\subseteq R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\subseteq R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Again the event: <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{R^{*}}(v)\geq rd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{R^{*}}(v)\geq rd</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by the choices of <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> for vertices <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> at distance at most <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, by (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>), this event is mutually independent of <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a fixed colour <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, each edge <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vw\in E(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vw\in E(v)</annotation></semantics></math> is independently included in <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{*}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{*}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> with probability</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\cdot\left(\frac{2\cdot\left\lfloor\frac{sd+7}{2}\right\rfloor}{K}\right)-\left(\frac{2\cdot\left\lfloor\frac{sd+7}{2}\right\rfloor}{K}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\cdot\left(\frac{2\cdot\left\lfloor\frac{sd+7}{2}\right\rfloor}{K}\right)-\left(\frac{2\cdot\left\lfloor\frac{sd+7}{2}\right\rfloor}{K}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, as the function <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=2x-x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=2x-x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing for <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\cdot\lfloor\frac{sd+7}{2}\rfloor/K\leq\frac{sd+7}{K}\leq\frac{sd+7}{kd}=\frac{s}{k}+\frac{7}{kd}&lt;0.1292" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.1292</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\cdot\lfloor\frac{sd+7}{2}\rfloor/K\leq\frac{sd+7}{K}\leq\frac{sd+7}{kd}=\frac{s}{k}+\frac{7}{kd}&lt;0.1292</annotation></semantics></math>,
this probability is bounded above by <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(0.1292)&lt;0.242" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.1292</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.242</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0.1292)&lt;0.242</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, for any fixed <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in[K]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in[K]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left(d_{R^{*}}(v)~|~C_{v}=C\right)&lt;0.242d=\mu_{r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.052em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.330em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0.242</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left(d_{R^{*}}(v)~|~C_{v}=C\right)&lt;0.242d=\mu_{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}=0.242" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.242</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}=0.242</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}=r-r_{1}=0.018" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.018</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}=r-r_{1}=0.018</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{r}=\frac{r_{2}}{r_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{r}=\frac{r_{2}}{r_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rd=(1+\delta_{r})\mu_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rd=(1+\delta_{r})\mu_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and by the Chernoff Bound, for any <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in[K]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in[K]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
