<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The analysis concerning <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> shall be different in at least two aspects.
First of all, for the sake of optimization of the lower bound for <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> within our argument, we shall not require the investigated event to be mutually independent of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> this time.
We however could not avoid some dependencies even if we did not strive to optimize our approach.
Thus, we are moreover forced to use a different concentration tool, i.e. the McDiarmid’s Inequality. In order to facilitate it efficiently, we shall have to be potentially more wasteful than above. Namely, while estimating <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{U}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{U}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> for the given vertex <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> we shall excessively take into account every neighbour of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> whose colour is repeated in the neighbourhood of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, even if there is no edge between the corresponding uniformly coloured neighbours of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us formally define the following superset of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(v)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U^{*}(v)=\{w\in N_{G}(v)~|~\exists w^{\prime}\in N_{G}(w)\cup N_{G}(v)\smallsetminus\{w\}:C_{w^{\prime}}=C_{w}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}(v)=\{w\in N_{G}(v)~|~\exists w^{\prime}\in N_{G}(w)\cup N_{G}(v)\smallsetminus\{w\}:C_{w^{\prime}}=C_{w}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that by (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>), the events in <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> are determined by colours assigned to vertices at distance at least <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. In order to bound the probability <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(|U^{*}(v)|\geq ud~|~\bigcap_{B\in\mathcal{B}}\overline{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋂</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(|U^{*}(v)|\geq ud~|~\bigcap_{B\in\mathcal{B}}\overline{B})</annotation></semantics></math> it is thus sufficient to provide some universal bound conditioning on any set of colours assigned to all vertices at distance at least <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. We shall additionally assume that the colour of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrarily fixed. Thus let us consider any event <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> fixing any specific colours for all vertices in <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\smallsetminus N_{G}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\smallsetminus N_{G}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> (such that <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\bigcap_{B\in\mathcal{B}}\overline{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋂</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\bigcap_{B\in\mathcal{B}}\overline{B}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us denote the neighbours of <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1},\ldots,w_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1},\ldots,w_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the fixed <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, the event: <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U^{*}(v)|\geq ud" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U^{*}(v)|\geq ud</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> independent random variables <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1},\ldots,W_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1},\ldots,W_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> assigning colours to <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1},\ldots,w_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1},\ldots,w_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, uniformly at random from <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[K]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[K]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be a binary variable which takes value <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if the colour of <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> appears at least twice in the neighbourhood of <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> (regardless of adjacency of the corresponding neighbours of <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>) or it is the same as the colour of any neighbour of <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> outside <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{G}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{G}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is valued <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise. Let</span></p>
