<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left(Z~|~A\right)\leq d\cdot\left(\frac{2}{k^{2}d}-\frac{1}{k^{4}d^{2}}\right)&lt;0.059d." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0.059</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left(Z~|~A\right)\leq d\cdot\left(\frac{2}{k^{2}d}-\frac{1}{k^{4}d^{2}}\right)&lt;0.059d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Note that changing the value of any single <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. the colour of <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, may change the value of <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> by at most <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (McDiarmid’s Inequality). ‣ 3. Tools ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, for <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1}=0.059" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.059</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1}=0.059</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{2}=u-u_{1}=0.072" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.072</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{2}=u-u_{1}=0.072</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
