<p id="S4.SS2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Once again, the last inequality above can be proven via setting <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{3}=e^{-(u_{2})^{2}/8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{3}=e^{-(u_{2})^{2}/8}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{u}(d)=d^{3}(u_{3})^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{u}(d)=d^{3}(u_{3})^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and noting that <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{u}(54000)&lt;0.11&lt;1/(3e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>54000</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.11</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{u}(54000)&lt;0.11&lt;1/(3e)</annotation></semantics></math>
while <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing for <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> at least <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/\ln(u_{3}^{-1})=24/(u_{2})^{2}&lt;4630" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4630</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/\ln(u_{3}^{-1})=24/(u_{2})^{2}&lt;4630</annotation></semantics></math>.
As <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U^{*}(v)|=Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U^{*}(v)|=Z</annotation></semantics></math>, by (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>) we thus obtain that:</span></p>
