<div id="S4.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S4.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>), (<a href="#S4.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>), (<a href="#S4.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>) the claim follows by the Lovász Local Lemma, i.e. Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7 (Lovász Local Lemma). ‣ 3. Tools ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3. </span>Decomposition of <math id="S4.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> to two similar subgraphs</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix any vertex colours assignment consistent with (i) – (iii) in Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Claim 10. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.
Basing on this we shall now colour the edges of <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> according to the following rules.
Note each of these regards a different subset of edges, which together partition <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="S4.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S4.I3.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S4.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We colour <math id="S4.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> any edge <math id="S4.I3.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vw\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vw\in S</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.I3.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{v}=I_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{v}=I_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. <math id="S4.I3.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{v}\neq O_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{v}\neq O_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S4.I3.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S4.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We colour <math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> any edge <math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vw\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vw\in S</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{v}=O_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{v}=O_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. <math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{v}\neq I_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{v}\neq I_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S4.I3.ix3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S4.I3.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The subgraph induced by the edges in <math id="S4.I3.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}\cup U^{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>e</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}\cup U^{e}</annotation></semantics></math> we colour according to Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 9. ‣ 3. Tools ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> using a constant function <math id="S4.I3.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\equiv 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\equiv 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S4.I3.ix4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S4.I3.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The subgraph induced by the edges in <math id="S4.I3.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\smallsetminus U^{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>e</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\smallsetminus U^{e}</annotation></semantics></math> we colour according to Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 9. ‣ 3. Tools ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> using a constant function <math id="S4.I3.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\equiv 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\equiv 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.ix5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S4.I3.ix5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S4.I3.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The subgraph induced by the (remaining) edges in <math id="S4.I3.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>
we colour according to Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 9. ‣ 3. Tools ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> using a constant function <math id="S4.I3.ix5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\equiv 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\equiv 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0,1</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote by <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i},U^{e}_{i},T_{i},S_{i},R_{i},R^{\prime}_{i},E^{\prime}_{i},E^{\prime\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i},U^{e}_{i},T_{i},S_{i},R_{i},R^{\prime}_{i},E^{\prime}_{i},E^{\prime\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the subsets of edges of <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E,U^{e},T,S,R,R^{\prime},E^{\prime},E^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>e</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E,U^{e},T,S,R,R^{\prime},E^{\prime},E^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, coloured <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also denote</p>
