<p id="S4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Note also that by (<a href="#S4.E12" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>), (<a href="#S4.E13" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.13</span></a>) and Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Claim 10. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>(iii),</p>
