<div id="S4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For every <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\smallsetminus U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\smallsetminus U</annotation></semantics></math>, the edges incident with <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in
<math id="S4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> can be partitioned as follows:
<math id="S4.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(v)=S(v)\cup R^{\prime}(v)\cup T(v)\cup E^{\prime\prime}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(v)=S(v)\cup R^{\prime}(v)\cup T(v)\cup E^{\prime\prime}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(v)=(T\smallsetminus U^{e})(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>e</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(v)=(T\smallsetminus U^{e})(v)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, analogously as above, by (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>), (<a href="#S4.E13" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.13</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E14" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.14</span></a>),</p>
