<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{E_{0}\smallsetminus S_{0}}(v)=d_{H_{0}}(v)-d_{S_{0}}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{E_{0}\smallsetminus S_{0}}(v)=d_{H_{0}}(v)-d_{S_{0}}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}\subseteq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}\subseteq S</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq d_{S_{0}}(v)\leq d_{S}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq d_{S_{0}}(v)\leq d_{S}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, by (<a href="#S4.E18" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.18</span></a>),</p>
<table id="S4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H_{0}}(v)\in\left[\frac{d-d_{S}(v)}{2}-3,\frac{d+d_{S}(v)}{2}+3\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H_{0}}(v)\in\left[\frac{d-d_{S}(v)}{2}-3,\frac{d+d_{S}(v)}{2}+3\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">By Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Claim 10. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>(i) we thus obtain that</p>
<table id="S4.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H_{0}}(v)\in\left(\frac{d-sd}{2}-3,\frac{d+sd}{2}+3\right)\hskip 14.22636pt{\rm for}\hskip 14.22636ptv\in V\smallsetminus U." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.42em;" width="1.42em"></mspace><mi>for</mi><mspace style="width:1.42em;" width="1.42em"></mspace><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H_{0}}(v)\in\left(\frac{d-sd}{2}-3,\frac{d+sd}{2}+3\right)\hskip 14.22636pt{\rm for}\hskip 14.22636ptv\in V\smallsetminus U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Note also that for every <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\smallsetminus U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\smallsetminus U</annotation></semantics></math>, by (<a href="#S4.E14" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.14</span></a>), Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Claim 10. ‣ 4.2. Assuring desired features of the distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In 4.1. Random colour assignment and distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>),</p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{H^{\prime}_{0}}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{H^{\prime}_{0}}(v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{E^{\prime}_{0}}(v)\geq d_{E^{\prime\prime}_{0}}(v)\geq\frac{d_{E^{\prime\prime}}(v)}{2}-1=\frac{d_{E\smallsetminus(S\cup T\cup R)}(v)}{2}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{E^{\prime}_{0}}(v)\geq d_{E^{\prime\prime}_{0}}(v)\geq\frac{d_{E^{\prime\prime}}(v)}{2}-1=\frac{d_{E\smallsetminus(S\cup T\cup R)}(v)}{2}-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d-d_{S}(v)-d_{T}(v)-d_{R}(v)}{2}-1&gt;\frac{d-sd-ud-rd}{2}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d-d_{S}(v)-d_{T}(v)-d_{R}(v)}{2}-1&gt;\frac{d-sd-ud-rd}{2}-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
