<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4. </span>A decomposition of <math id="S4.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to two locally irregular subgraphs</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="S4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}=\frac{d}{6}-\frac{sd}{3}-\frac{ud}{6}-\frac{13}{3}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}=\frac{d}{6}-\frac{sd}{3}-\frac{ud}{6}-\frac{13}{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{0,1,\ldots,\lceil d_{1}\rceil-1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{0,1,\ldots,\lceil d_{1}\rceil-1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D|\geq d_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D|\geq d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In 4.1. Random colour assignment and distinguished sets ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>),</p>
<table id="S4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{ud}{2}+1\leq d_{1}\leq\frac{d-ud}{2}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{ud}{2}+1\leq d_{1}\leq\frac{d-ud}{2}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, by (<a href="#S4.E16" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.16</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E17" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.17</span></a>),</p>
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{U^{e}_{0}}(v)&lt;|D|\hskip 14.22636pt{\rm and}\hskip 14.22636ptd_{T_{0}\smallsetminus U^{e}_{0}}(v)&gt;\lceil d_{1}\rceil-1\hskip 14.22636pt{\rm for}\hskip 14.22636ptv\in U." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>e</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:1.42em;" width="1.42em"></mspace><mi>and</mi><mspace style="width:1.42em;" width="1.42em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>e</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1.42em;" width="1.42em"></mspace><mi>for</mi><mspace style="width:1.42em;" width="1.42em"></mspace><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{U^{e}_{0}}(v)&lt;|D|\hskip 14.22636pt{\rm and}\hskip 14.22636ptd_{T_{0}\smallsetminus U^{e}_{0}}(v)&gt;\lceil d_{1}\rceil-1\hskip 14.22636pt{\rm for}\hskip 14.22636ptv\in U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For every vertex <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in U</annotation></semantics></math> we choose any subset <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> of the set of edges <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}(v)\smallsetminus U^{e}_{0}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}(v)\smallsetminus U^{e}_{0}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="S4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T_{v}|\in D" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T_{v}|\in D</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">so that</p>
<table id="S4.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H_{0}}(v)-|T_{v}|\neq d_{H_{0}}(w)-|T_{w}|\hskip 14.22636pt{\rm for~every}\hskip 14.22636ptvw\in U^{e}_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.42em;" width="1.42em"></mspace><mrow><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>every</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1.42em;" width="1.42em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>e</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H_{0}}(v)-|T_{v}|\neq d_{H_{0}}(w)-|T_{w}|\hskip 14.22636pt{\rm for~every}\hskip 14.22636ptvw\in U^{e}_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#S4.E23" title="In 4.4. A decomposition of 𝐻_0 to two locally irregular subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.23</span></a>) we may do this greedily, analysing one vertex in <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> after another.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="S4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{U}=\bigcup_{v\in U}T_{v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{U}=\bigcup_{v\in U}T_{v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Set</p>
<table id="S4.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=2K." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=2K.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">With every <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\smallsetminus U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\smallsetminus U</annotation></semantics></math> we associate an integer <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(v)\in\{0,1,\ldots,\lambda-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(v)\in\{0,1,\ldots,\lambda-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{T_{U}\cup R_{0}}(v)+t(v)\equiv 2O_{v}\pmod{\lambda}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{T_{U}\cup R_{0}}(v)+t(v)\equiv 2O_{v}\pmod{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Note that by (<a href="#S4.E20" title="In 4.3. Decomposition of 𝐺 to two similar subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.20</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E26" title="In 4.4. A decomposition of 𝐻_0 to two locally irregular subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.26</span></a>), <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H^{\prime}_{0}}(v)&gt;6\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H^{\prime}_{0}}(v)&gt;6\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\smallsetminus U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\smallsetminus U</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus we may apply Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 3. Tools ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> to <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\prime}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\prime}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{v}=\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{v}=\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\smallsetminus U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\smallsetminus U</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t:V\smallsetminus U\to\{0,1,\ldots,\lambda-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t:V\smallsetminus U\to\{0,1,\ldots,\lambda-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> fulfilling (<a href="#S4.E27" title="In 4.4. A decomposition of 𝐻_0 to two locally irregular subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.27</span></a>).
The resulting subgraph of <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\prime}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\prime}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> we denote by <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 3. Tools ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and (<a href="#S4.E27" title="In 4.4. A decomposition of 𝐻_0 to two locally irregular subgraphs ‣ 4. Proof of Theorem ‣ Decomposability of regular graphs to 4 locally irregular subgraphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.27</span></a>), for every <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\smallsetminus U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\smallsetminus U</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{H}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{H}(v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\frac{d_{H^{\prime}_{0}}(v)}{3},\frac{2d_{H^{\prime}_{0}}(v)}{3}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\frac{d_{H^{\prime}_{0}}(v)}{3},\frac{2d_{H^{\prime}_{0}}(v)}{3}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{H}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{H}(v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≡</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t(v),t(v)+1\pmod{\lambda}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t(v),t(v)+1\pmod{\lambda},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">where the latter means that <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent either to <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(v)</annotation></semantics></math> or to <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(v)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(v)+1</annotation></semantics></math> modulo <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
We finally define a decomposition of <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}=(V,E(F_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}=(V,E(F_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{2}=(V,E(F_{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}=(V,E(F_{2}))</annotation></semantics></math> by setting:</p>
